// The engine's native seams -- the window, present and input (gfx), and the
// files assets are read from (fs) -- are the standard library's backends, so
// this manifest imports nothing, and neither does a project using the engine.

// The engine's constants. Each is a program global read with (import name).
//
// inp_kmax: key codes tracked, 0-255 character keys and 256-511 the rest. The
// guard on a key code in core/sys/inp is not optional: an out-of-range list
// store aborts the process, and nothing in the seam's contract promises a
// backend will never widen its range.
//
// asset_chunk: 64 KB per read -- big enough that the per-call cost disappears,
// small enough that the staging list is a rounding error against the file.
//
// zst_lmax: the zstd literals buffer's size. A block decompresses to at most
// 128 KiB, so its literals cannot exceed that either; allocating for the worst
// case once is 128 KB of store against an allocation per block, in a language
// where nothing is ever given back.
//
// tin_base: text entry's base duration in ms (docs/NAMES.md), and itself the
// caret's blink half-period: solid for 400 ms, dark for 400 ms. It is the same
// number as the rest of the family on purpose -- one duration is what makes a
// field feel like one thing, and a blink that beat against the repeat rate
// would look like a fault.
//
// ast_kbase: the AST node kind family's base (docs/NAMES.md), 100. The
// individual kinds are now conf.id constants rather than functions.
//
// lex_kbase: the token kind family's base (docs/NAMES.md), 11. The
// individual kinds are now conf.id constants rather than functions.
//
// d2_clear: the transparency convention. A sprite pixel of -1 means "do not
// write". A packed colour is 0xRRGGBB, so every real colour is 0 .. 16777215
// and -1 cannot collide with one -- which is the whole reason to pick it rather
// than, say, magenta, the classic colour key that a game then cannot use.
// IDML_GAME.md section 2's `. clear` in a palette decodes to this value.
//
// txt_first: the first code point any face here has a glyph for -- and, by
// convention, the first frame of a sprite font (IDML_GAME.md section 2's `from
// 32`). This is still a bare-looking literal while its neighbours read txt_st,
// and that is the point: it is not a property of the loaded face but a fact
// about the engine. A loaded PSF is stored from 32 upward whatever its own
// indexing was (glyph/face/put.id), so txt_num_sc can go on spelling '0' as
// (import txt_first) + 16 whatever face is loaded.
int inp_kmax = 512;
int asset_chunk = 65536;
int zst_lmax = 131072;
int tin_base = 400;
int ast_kbase = 100;
int lex_kbase = 11;
int d2_clear = 0 - 1;
int txt_first = 32;
int ast_k_nil = 100;
int ast_k_file = 101;
int ast_k_import = 102;
int ast_k_palette = 103;
int ast_k_pcol = 104;
int ast_k_sprite = 105;
int ast_k_model = 106;
int ast_k_game = 107;
